  "body": "The post-merge gate (batch tier, parallel lanes since #2788) now takes about 16 minutes for its gate step (run for `83c53732b`, down from 26 minutes for `3ffe2338f` after #2939 and #2757). The lanes run in parallel, so the gate cannot finish before its single longest test target.\n\nThe longest targets in the run for `83c53732b`:\n\n| Target | Time | Tests over 60 s |\n|---|---|---|\n| `motion suites: lib` | 567 s | 7, all in `machining2d::adaptive_troch::tests` (`custom_parameters_reach_parallel_and_closed_lane_layouts`, `custom_return_feed_is_emitted_by_production_parallel_lanes_and_cleanup`, `explicit_trochoidal_parameters_control_engagement_return_feed_and_loop_width`, `pocket_with_island_is_cleared_without_crossing_or_excess_rest`, `ring_round_island_is_cleared_with_closed_lane`, `triangle_and_wide_to_narrow_neck_are_cleared`, `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes`) |\n| `app suites: keep_law` | 253 s | 1 |\n| `app suites: adaptive_trochoid` | 208 s | 4 |\n| `motion suites: rest_adaptive` | 198 s | 2 |\n\nThe `motion` lib target is more than twice as long as the next one. AGENTS.md \"Testing\" says a test over about 60 s in debug moves to the heavy lane or gets a slimmer fixture.\n\nOptions (for the worker to choose and record in `docs/decisions/`):\n1. Give the seven `adaptive_troch` tests slimmer fixtures (smaller pockets, a coarser tolerance) that still pin the same behaviour.\n2. Move the full-size versions to the heavy lane with a light twin each (the light tier of #2787).\n3. Move the `adaptive_troch` tests into their own test target, so the lane scheduler can run them beside the rest of `motion` lib.\n\nCoverage must not drop: the `#[test]` count stays the same, and the asserts of each moved test are kept.\n\nDone means: no single target in the batch tier takes more than about 300 s on the post-merge runner, and the `motion` lib target's time is recorded before and after on this issue.\n",
